{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"F24 assessment completed. The post import check belongs to rebar fsck in the current codebase because fsck reads event bytes and Git refs and is read-only by default. Rebar doctor currently checks dependency links, dirty tracker artifacts, locks, and mapping configuration. The canonical doctor epic remains an idea that proposes adding fsck as a future category. Hexametral-peppery-wasp explicitly preserved fsck as the store integrity command. The proposed F24 edit remains a one line checklist correction from validate to fsck, without a redundant dry-run flag. F24 remains deferred pending operator approval."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787600971137747001,"uuid":"15da5b2b-ca7a-46db-9bd5-2d01d0402c84"}